                  "doc_id": "RSE-PTO-01",
                  "title": "Paid Time Off Policy",
                  "section": "4.2",
                  "section_heading": "Notice",
                  "text": "Requests for more than 3 PTO days need at least 14 calendar days' notice (two weeks) before the first day off. Requests of 3 PTO days or fewer have no minimum notice: submit them as early as practical. Count only the PTO days charged, not weekends or company holidays.\nNotice is counted from the day you submit the request to the first day off. For example, a request submitted on a Monday for a full working week off starting two Mondays later meets the notice rule; the same request submitted the Friday before does not. A late request is not automatically declined, but your manager may decline it if the team can't cover your work.",
                  "score": 0.032
